1
00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:05.940
[S01] I've lived more in my head than I've lived in real life.

2
00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:12.750
[S01] Most of my suffering comes from my own head. Most of my enjoyment comes from

3
00:00:14.039 --> 00:00:19.140
[S01] a delusional reality that I've made up in which doesn't actually exist.

4
00:00:21.059 --> 00:00:22.170
[S01] I tend to

5
00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:30.179
[S01] overanalyze events that have happened over and over again, you know, you know, replaying conversations

6
00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:35.670
[S01] that already happened. I also practice conversations that will probably never happen.

7
00:00:36.359 --> 00:00:38.719
[S01] I like to imagine success

8
00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:40.469
[S01] in my head

9
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.140
[S01] of places that I'll be.

10
00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:48.689
[S01] And it literally gives me a feeling of excitement or dopamine as though I've actually gone out

11
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.700
[S01] and achieved that thing.

12
00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:59.039
[S01] It's not just daydreaming. It's like running full simulations.

13
00:01:00.119 --> 00:01:02.850
[S01] Full scenarios are like a future

14
00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:05.400
[S01] that doesn't actually exist.

15
00:01:07.019 --> 00:01:10.560
[S01] Because of this, I feel like real life is secondary

16
00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.730
[S01] to the one that I've created in my head.

17
00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.079
[S01] And this, this

18
00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:18.870
[S01] saying this stuff out loud makes me sound

19
00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:24.150
[S01] almost schizophrenic or something, but I have a feeling a lot of other people relate to this.

20
00:01:25.829 --> 00:01:30.750
[S01] In your head, you know, you, you control the outcomes. There's no rejection. There's no embarrassment or failure.

21
00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:32.730
[S01] You kind of get what you want.

22
00:01:33.689 --> 00:01:34.890
[S01] You can even be

23
00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:39.120
[S01] funnier, smarter. You can be a more confident person.

24
00:01:40.109 --> 00:01:46.049
[S01] You can sort of detach from the pressure of whatever it is you want to do when you live in your head.

25
00:01:46.769 --> 00:01:52.290
[S01] And that's what's so nice about it. And that's why it's like, it's so easy to fall into that trap. You know what I mean?

26
00:01:54.030 --> 00:02:01.079
[S01] But there, there's a hitting cost to it. You know, you miss real opportunities because you hesitate too long.

27
00:02:02.519 --> 00:02:04.620
[S01] Your confidence, it stays low

28
00:02:05.069 --> 00:02:09.539
[S01] because you're not getting the real feedback and everything is like fake dopamine.

29
00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.909
[S01] And so life starts to feel dull.

30
00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:19.159
[S01] And it's not necessarily that it is. It's just you're not, you're not trying to optimize in your life.

31
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.879
[S01] You know, you start identifying as an over thinker.

32
00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:30.900
[S01] And this becomes some type of excuse to avoid actual action, actual change.

33
00:02:31.159 --> 00:02:33.629
[S01] And so you convince yourself that you're preparing

34
00:02:34.259 --> 00:02:35.659
[S01] when you're actually avoiding.

35
00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.909
[S01] But for me, I reached this weird realization moment where

36
00:02:43.259 --> 00:02:46.560
[S01] you imagined entire phases of life

37
00:02:47.159 --> 00:02:48.719
[S01] that never actually

38
00:02:49.259 --> 00:02:50.460
[S01] have been lived out.

39
00:02:50.909 --> 00:02:53.729
[S01] And so you start to look back and you start to notice

40
00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:57.840
[S01] how little you actually did in comparison to what you imagined.

41
00:02:58.289 --> 00:02:59.400
[S01] And that's the issue.

42
00:02:59.909 --> 00:03:03.030
[S01] Feeling like time has passed, but nothing has really happened.

43
00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:04.620
[S01] And

44
00:03:06.629 --> 00:03:10.110
[S01] I'm trying to actively make a change with that. I'm trying to

45
00:03:11.969 --> 00:03:14.189
[S01] turn my visualizations from

46
00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:23.610
[S01] imaginary to almost more of like a manifestation where I'm putting energy towards trying to actualize that and turn it into my real life reality.

47
00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.120
[S01] That is, that's what you need to do. You need to culminate that.

48
00:03:27.629 --> 00:03:34.830
[S01] So there's a turning point, right? Like you, you have to understand that clarity doesn't, doesn't come from thinking. It actually comes from doing.

49
00:03:35.069 --> 00:03:38.490
[S01] I recently made a video about this where I talked about, you know,

50
00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.979
[S01] therapy and how I think therapy.

51
00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:45.240
[S01] The problem with it is that all you do is overanalyze. You don't actually take action.

52
00:03:45.629 --> 00:03:47.789
[S01] And so you sort of ruminate on your thoughts.

53
00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.719
[S01] And that causes you to oftentimes

54
00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.270
[S01] be more in your problems.

55
00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:56.069
[S01] And you don't

56
00:03:58.169 --> 00:04:01.680
[S01] take any practical steps at making change in your life.

57
00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.560
[S01] So, so that's the problem, right?

58
00:04:06.419 --> 00:04:09.030
[S01] Real life is always going to be messier than your thoughts.

59
00:04:11.039 --> 00:04:11.580
[S01] But

60
00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:16.470
[S01] that's okay. There's sort of a peace in accepting this. You have to, you have to embrace it.

61
00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.350
[S01] Those are my thoughts. Thank you guys for watching.
